2010 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The fast development of the Internet of Things \050IoT\051 has led to billions of devices being interconnected through the use of networks\056 IPv6 becomes increasingly important for IoT due to the possibility of providing a huge amount of addresses for the numerous devices that should be able to connect to networks\056\n\nHowever\054 due to the IPv6 privacy features\054 devices may change their addresses from time to time\056 Even though address rotation helps increase privacy\054 it makes it more complicated for the IoT security monitoring systems to recognize the device after the change\056\n\nIn addition\054 the IoT networks may include devices with different capabilities\054 software\054 and security settings\056 In case of an intrusion\054 an unauthorized device will communicate in a suspicious way\054 generate abnormal traffic\054 and try to interact with other devices\056\n\nThat is why it is necessary to develop a security solution that would be capable of keeping track of the IoT devices despite the IPv6 address changes while decreasing the unnecessary disclosure of the device identity and sensitive data\056\n\nThe aim of our project is the development of a web\055based\054 privacy\055aware IPv6 IoT security monitoring platform\056 The platform includes IPv6 monitoring\054 device identity correlation\054 behavioral analysis\054 rogue\055device detection risks\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 2011 0 R
     /Pg 514 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

