2035 0 obj
  << /ActualText (PRIV6\055SHIELD can be optimized to provide faster threat detection while reducing unnecessary data collection and false alerts\056\nLightweight Local Processing\072 Analyze IPv6 and ICMPv6 traffic locally instead of sending raw network data to external services\056\nAdaptive NDP Thresholds\072 Dynamically adjust the normal NDP traffic baseline according to the current IoT network activity to reduce false positives\056\nEfficient Pseudonym Management\072 Use short\055lived pseudonyms with automatic expiration so unnecessary identity mappings are not retained\056\nEvent\055Based Monitoring\072 Process important security events rather than storing every packet indefinitely\054 reducing processing and storage requirements\056\nFast Rogue\055RA Detection\072 Maintain a local list of authorized router information so unauthorized Router Advertisements can be detected quickly\056\nLocal Event Correlation\072 Combine related events such as address rotation and abnormal NDP activity before generating an alert\054 preventing duplicate notifications\056\nReal\055Time Dashboard Optimization\072 Use WebSockets to send only relevant security events to the dashboard instead of repeatedly refreshing the complete dataset\056\nPrivacy\055by\055Design Storage\072 Store only the minimum information required for security analysis and automatically remove expired session\057pseudonym information\056\nScalable Architecture\072 Keep packet capture\054 privacy management\054 detection\054 backend\054 and dashboard as separate modules so additional IoT devices and detection rules can be added later\056\nPerformance Evaluation\072 Continuously evaluate detection rate\054 false\055positive rate\054 pseudonym expiration\054 and address\055rotation handling to tune the system\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 2036 0 R
     /Pg 1222 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

